T = {
    "930": "7.5. Future Research Directions on Judgment\u2013Decision Transitions",

    "931": "This study meticulously examined, through a single-case qualitative study and process tracing, the process by which judgments formed within organizations after AI utilization training requests fail to lead to decision-making. As a result, it was confirmed that the pattern in which the judgment\u2013decision transition is interrupted arises not from simple implementation delay but from the conjunction of specific processual and structural conditions. These findings provide a scholarly foundation for expanding the judgment\u2013decision transition into an independent research domain. Accordingly, this section presents the major research agendas that future studies may deepen.",

    "932": "First, rather than treating the failure of the judgment\u2013decision transition as a singular phenomenon, future research may examine the typologization of non-decision states as a core research agenda. Although this study analyzed the state in which decision-making did not occur despite the existence of judgments as a single processual phenomenon, in actual organizations, non-decision states are likely to manifest in diverse forms and along different pathways. For example, cases in which judgments formed after AI utilization training requests are deferred for a period and then dissolve, cases in which they are marginalized by other agendas, and cases in which they are repeatedly discussed but never connected to formal decisions may each harbor distinct structural conditions and mechanisms. Therefore, follow-up studies may typologize these non-decision states and, by comparing and analyzing the organizational and institutional conditions under which each type arises, more precisely explicate the micro-level manifestations of judgment\u2013decision transition failure.",

    "933": "Second, multi-case comparative research that cross-validates how the conversion mechanism between judgment and decision varies according to the distinctive context of the macro-level organizational ecosystem is urgently called for. Although this inquiry anatomized the processual stagnation observed within the specific terrain of a nonprofit religious organization, rigorous empirical verification is required as to whether such an intransigent trajectory of disconnection would be identically reproduced within entirely different structural forms. Future scholarly endeavors must employ the boundary between for-profit and nonprofit entities, organizational scale, and the degree of centralization of decision-making authority as core analytical criteria to three-dimensionally elucidate under what structural conditions judgments gestated after AI utilization training requests dissolve or leap into complete decisions. Such cross-sectional comparative analysis will provide a decisive foundation for theoretically determining whether the Seizing phase of Dynamic Capabilities is an indiscriminate \u2018universal capability\u2019 manifested in any environment or a highly \u2018contingent capability\u2019 that is thoroughly bound to and manifested through context.",

    "934": "Third, an in-depth dissection of the structural function performed by the so-called \u2018coordinator\u2019 or institutional mediator at the juncture of transition\u2014where gestated judgments are propelled onto the trajectory of full-fledged decision-making\u2014must necessarily follow. As was clearly confirmed in the preceding empirical trajectory, the evaporation of a dedicated agent to seize normative judgments anchored after AI utilization training requests and launch them into the formal decision-making network was directly linked to the fatal morass of conversion stagnation. Therefore, follow-up studies must meticulously trace how the overall trajectory of transition dynamics unfolds when \u2018mediating authority\u2019\u2014which gathers fragmented field-level judgments, logically reassembles them, and elevates them as agenda items to formal deliberative bodies\u2014is institutionally and explicitly conferred. Such scholarly inquiry is expected to ultimately yield the outcome of forging, in the most systematic theoretical language, the authority distribution structure and pluralistic coordination mechanisms operating in the depths of the Seizing mechanism.",

    "935": "Fourth, longitudinal tracking research centered on the concept of the \u2018Judgment Life Cycle\u2019 is needed. The Judgment Life Cycle refers to the temporal unfolding process from the formation of a judgment through its immediate conversion into a decision, its deferral for a certain period, its displacement by another agenda, or its complete dissolution. By tracking judgments formed after AI utilization training requests over extended periods, the conditions under which judgments are reignited or excluded can be analyzed, and this will serve as a foundation for more precisely explaining the temporal dynamics of the Seizing stage.",

    "936": "Fifth, follow-up research needs to explore the organizational learning effect left behind by the experience of judgment\u2013decision transition failure. In this study, the non-decision state persisted; however, whether such an experience exerts influence on the organization\u2019s response patterns or institutional design in subsequent similar judgment situations remains a matter for additional analysis. Future studies may analyze how the experience of failing to translate into decisions after AI utilization training requests is subsequently reflected in improvements to the organization\u2019s decision-making structure or procedural design, thereby exploring the conditions under which the non-decision state can be converted not as a simple failure but as a potential learning resource for the organization.",

    "937": "In synthesis, the core of the future research agenda presented by this study does not lie in extending the effectiveness of AI utilization training to performance indicators. Rather, it lies in presenting the research possibilities for deepening the processual phenomenon of the judgment\u2013decision transition as a domain of analysis, centered on the question of why and how judgments fail to convert into decisions after AI utilization training requests. Such studies will contribute not only to the theoretical refinement of the Seizing mechanism but also to more three-dimensionally illuminating the structural and institutional conditions required for organizations to generate actual change following AI utilization training requests.",

    "938": "7.6. Overall Contributions and Implications",

    "939": "This chapter synthesizes the analytical findings and discussions of this study and concludes the dissertation as a whole by organizing the managerial significance of the disconnection phenomenon between judgments and decisions occurring in organizations after AI utilization training requests. This study is explicitly identified not as research that verifies the outcomes of AI utilization training or measures the magnitude of training effects, but as research that analyzes at the mechanism level\u2014within the theoretical framework of the operating conditions of the Seizing stage of Dynamic Capabilities Theory\u2014the conditions under which judgments formed within organizations after training requests fail to convert into formal decision-making and stagnate.",

    "940": "The case analysis revealed that, although organizational-level judgments clearly existed, a phenomenon was observed in which judgments failed to convert into decision-making and were maintained in a state of non-decision when minimum structural conditions\u2014such as the designation of responsible agents, schedule setting, and procedure initiation\u2014remained unfulfilled. These findings raise the necessity of understanding the Seizing stage not as the outcome of a singular decision act, but as the entire processual configuration through which judgments are incorporated into or excluded from the organization\u2019s decision-making structure, departing from existing perspectives.",

    "941": "From a theoretical standpoint, this study expands the explanatory scope of Dynamic Capabilities Theory by redefining Seizing not as a \u2018moment of decision\u2019 but as a \u2018processual mechanism.\u2019 In particular, by analyzing the state in which judgments are not converted into decisions not as a reduction to individual competency deficits or failures of training effectiveness, but as a problem of organizational-level structural conditions and procedural arrangements, it presents a structural and processual interpretive frame that explains the gap between AI utilization training requests and organizational performance.",

    "942": "Viewed from the practical stratum, this inquiry draws a clear demarcation against the prevailing myopic approach that has sought to measure the repercussions generated by AI utilization training requests solely through the completeness of fragmented educational curricula or the magnitude of individual learners\u2019 technical proficiency gains. For judgments gestated within the organizational system to leap toward substantive organizational transformation, an \u2018institutional pathway\u2019 to channel those judgments into the formal decision-making network must be meticulously constructed in advance. That is, this study has unequivocally demonstrated that robust structural devices\u2014such as the explicit designation of authorized responsible agents, the institutionalization of review processes, and the coordination of concrete implementation timelines\u2014function as indispensable launch conditions propelling the judgment\u2013decision-making conversion. Such an innovative perspective rescues a phenomenon previously dismissed as a mere transient learning event and comprehensively repositions it as a highly \u2018strategic intervention\u2019 that must be vigorously coupled with the macro-level decision system of the organizational ecosystem.",

    "943": "At this juncture, the strategic intervention as named by this study is by no means a narrow concept merely designating the visible educational program itself. Rather, it precisely targets a \u2018macro-level organizational design act\u2019 that artificially weaves and coordinates the essential structural conditions so that normative judgments anchored after AI utilization training requests may be safely emplaced onto the trajectory of formal decision-making. The definitive conclusion is that this original concept will function as the most powerful \u2018conceptual framework\u2019 for incisively dissecting and specifying the core mechanisms of organizational design that pry open the previously sealed threshold of the judgment\u2013decision-making conversion, transcending far beyond the dimension of piecemeal operational manuals or micro-level management techniques.",

    "944": "The core scholarly contributions of this study may be summarized as follows.",

    "945": "First, this study expanded Dynamic Capabilities Theory from a processual perspective by re-conceptualizing Seizing not as an act but as a process.",

    "946": "Second, it theorized the failure of outcome conversion after AI utilization training requests not as a problem of individuals or training effectiveness, but as a problem of the organization\u2019s decision-making structure and procedural conditions.\nThird, by placing non-decision and non-events at the center of analysis, it presented\u2014as a theoretically legitimated unit of analysis\u2014the stagnation state of organizational change that prior management research had failed to capture.",

    "947": "In synthesis, this study, rather than defining the gap between AI utilization training requests and organizational performance as a result of failure, presents it as an interpretive framework that analytically reveals the structural and processual conditions required for the activation of organizational Dynamic Capabilities\u2014particularly the Seizing mechanism. From this perspective, this study presents the managerial explanatory possibilities connecting education, technology, organizational design, and decision-making structure, and concludes the dissertation by enabling follow-up research and practical discussions centered on the core mechanism of the judgment\u2013decision-making transition.",

    "948": "Abstract",

    "949": "Chapter 1, the Introduction, elevates as the most critical research problem of this inquiry the fatal disconnection phenomenon whereby, despite the vigorous proliferation of AI utilization training requests within organizational ecosystems, their repercussions fail to leap onto the trajectory of substantive decision-making networks and execution, instead evaporating entirely. In other words, this dissertation does not confine itself to the retrospective evaluative exercise of quantifying performance indicators of fragmented educational curricula or verifying piecemeal learning effectiveness. Rather, it precisely calibrates the analytical zero-point to dissecting the blind spots of the \u2018conversion mechanism\u2019 that prevent judgments firmly gestated within the organizational depths\u2014immediately after an AI utilization training request is initiated\u2014from crossing the threshold into formal decision-making.",

    "950": "As the logical framework for penetrating this weighty scholarly question, this study adopts Dynamic Capabilities Theory as its robust theoretical foundation. In particular, it maximizes research density through the strategy of deliberately bracketing the Sensing phase\u2014which reads environmental turbulence\u2014and the Transforming phase\u2014which comprehensively redeploys resources\u2014while strictly confining the analytical lens to the depths of the Seizing stage alone. The ultimate scholarly orientation of this inquiry lies in elucidating the concrete trajectory along which judgments are constructed within the organizational system and the intransigent structural and processual conditions that frustrate those judgments at the juncture of their transition into complete decision-making. In conclusion, the three core research questions threading through this dissertation are perfectly organized in the direction of meticulously formulating the terrain of judgment gestation, the micro-level operating mechanisms of the disconnection that blocks conversion, and the eventual processual reconceptualization of the Seizing stage.",

    "951": "This chapter also clarifies the scope and limitations of the research, intentionally excluding individual capabilities, technological performance comparisons, and outcome measurement, and confining the analysis to organizational-level judgment structures and conversion processes. Methodologically, by adopting a single-case qualitative study design, it makes explicit that the aim is not statistical generalization but theoretical generalization, and provides a logical starting point for the theoretical, methodological, and analytical discussions in subsequent chapters.",

    "952": "Chapter 2, the Literature Review, systematically reviews prior research on Dynamic Capabilities Theory, organizational learning, and decision-making to form the theoretical foundation of this study. It first summarizes that, within Dynamic Capabilities Theory, performance is shaped not by resource possession but by the processual capabilities of sensing\u2013seizing\u2013transforming in response to environmental change, and critically reviews how existing studies have predominantly treated the Seizing stage as an outcome of strategic choice.",

    "953": "Additionally, by re-examining organizational learning theory and the Knowing\u2013Doing Gap discourse, it theoretically confirms that a structural gap exists between knowledge acquired through organizational learning or formed judgments and their execution as action. Studies addressing AI adoption and utilization have also noted that disconnections repeatedly occur between individual-level competency enhancement and organizational-level implementation changes; however, processual explanations of how judgments traverse specific pathways to convert into or stagnate as decisions have remained relatively limited. Accordingly, Chapter 2 theoretically justifies the necessity of analyzing the micro-level operating conditions and processual structure of the Seizing stage in order to interpret the phenomenon in which judgments fail to lead to decision-making despite having been formed after AI utilization training requests, and concretizes the analytical focus of this study.",

    "954": "Chapter 3, the Methodology, systematically presents the validity and analytical strategy of the qualitative single-case study design adopted by this research. This study places at the center of analysis not the failure of decision-making, but the state in which decision-making was never initiated (non-decision, non-event), and therefore selected a qualitative case study design suitable for process-centered exploration rather than outcome-centered approaches.",

    "955": "This inquiry firmly positions the single case under analysis as a \u2018revelatory case\u2019 that exposes concealed mechanisms, and adopted \u2018process tracing\u2019 as the core analytical tool for in-depth micro-level analysis of the pathways through which judgments gestated after AI utilization training requests become mired in stagnation. Furthermore, it transparently disclosed that the researcher herself was positioned as a participant observer within the organizational ecosystem who captured field data, yet occupied a position devoid of substantive final decision-making authority, thereby rigorously controlling the structural conditions and limitations that may accompany the interpretive process.",

    "956": "The collection of specific empirical data was conducted through the three-dimensional cross-weaving of pluralistic data sources\u2014ranging from official internal organizational communications, electronic approval system histories, meeting minutes and work records, to field participant observation memos\u2014and scholarly credibility of interpretation was maximized through rigorous triangulation. In comprehensive terms, this chapter unequivocally demonstrates that such a meticulously designed methodological trajectory constitutes the most perfectly aligned logical conclusion for achieving the ultimate orientation of this inquiry: the dissection of the non-activation mechanism by which the Seizing phase of Dynamic Capabilities Theory ultimately fails to awaken.",

    "957": "The ensuing Chapter 4, the Case Analysis, fully reassembles\u2014based on empirical evidence\u2014the trajectories of judgment and decision that existed within the organizational system immediately after the field-level AI utilization training request was initiated. Through multilayered analysis, it forges as the most critical empirical finding the fatal disconnection phenomenon whereby, despite organizational-level judgments having been clearly gestated and shared among members, they failed to leap onto the stage of formal decision-making or yield any substantive resource allocation outcomes.",

    "958": "The inner landscape of the field, viewed through the lens of precise process tracing, is all the more starkly revealed. Despite the complete absence of overt resistance toward or externalized internal conflict over the gestated judgments, the procedures for incorporation into the formal decision-making network were never activated, and ultimately the entire matter was deferred and stagnated amid prolonged silence. This by no means signifies that a \u2018deficiency of judgment\u2019 occurred within the organization; rather, it powerfully suggests that a vacuum state in which complete decisions could not be gestated\u2014despite the firm existence of established judgments\u2014was being vigorously preserved by structural forces.",

    "959": "Such critical empirical insights thoroughly exclude the superficial attempt to reduce the conversion frustration observed after AI utilization training requests to deficits in the execution capabilities of fragmented operational staff or insufficient piecemeal outcome generation. The overwhelming conclusion converges instead upon the three-dimensional demonstration\u2014through item-by-item field evidence\u2014that an intransigent \u2018processual bottleneck\u2019 lurked at the very heart of the macro-level structural network connecting gestated judgments to substantive decision-making within the organizational ecosystem.",

    "960": "Chapter 5, Discussion: Processual Theoretical Elaboration of the Seizing Mechanism, theoretically repositions the empirical findings of Chapter 4 from the perspective of Dynamic Capabilities Theory, particularly the Seizing stage. This chapter critiques the existing assumption that an automatic and inevitable continuity exists between judgment and decision-making, and demonstrates that a state in which the process has not been initiated (non-activation) can be structurally sustained between the two.",

    "961": "The stagnation of the judgment\u2013decision-making transition is interpreted as having occurred not as a result of explicit opposition or failure, but because the institutional and processual triggers required to incorporate judgments formed after AI utilization training requests into formal decision-making procedures were not activated. Accordingly, Seizing is re-conceptualized not as a resultant event or decision-making ability, but as a processual mechanism that converts judgments into decisions.",

    "962": "This chapter theoretically formalizes that the Seizing stage is activated only under specific conditions, thereby supplementing and extending the micro-foundations of Dynamic Capabilities Theory. Through this formalization, it theorizes the judgment\u2013decision transition stagnation phenomenon not as failure but as a state of process non-initiation, and establishes the theoretical groundwork for the comprehensive contribution discussion to be presented in the concluding chapter.",

    "964": "Conclusion",

    "965": "Chapter 6, Conclusion and Implications, elucidated why judgments formed within organizations after AI utilization training requests fail to convert into actual decision-making and organizational performance\u2014not from the perspective of the success or failure of outcomes, but from the perspective of the non-activation mechanism of the judgment\u2013decision conversion process. Analysis revealed that, in the case organization, despite the clear formal and informal existence of organizational-level judgments regarding the necessity of AI utilization training, a state of non-decision in which decision-making did not occur was structurally sustained because minimum processual conditions\u2014such as the designation of responsible agents, the initiation of formal procedures, and the establishment of timelines and accountability\u2014were not activated.",

    "966": "Such empirical findings thoroughly dismantle the pre-existing scholarly premise that blindly assumed gestated judgments would directly leap to substantive decisions. Furthermore, they unequivocally demonstrate that the frustration of outcome generation originated not from a mere \u2018deficiency of judgment\u2019 or the \u2018limitations of fragmented educational curricula,\u2019 but from a \u2018fatal blind spot in organizational configuration\u2019 in which the procedural and structural conditions that must be activated immediately following the anchoring of judgments were fundamentally paralyzed.",

    "967": "Drawing upon such multilayered analysis as a robust foundation, this inquiry boldly departed from the inertia of treating the Seizing phase posited by Dynamic Capabilities Theory as merely a product of retrospective strategic resolution or visible resource commitment. Instead, it achieved the weighty theoretical accomplishment of comprehensively re-conceptualizing Seizing as a \u2018vigorous combination of processual conditions\u2019 that must be interlocked and activated to channel constructed normative judgments onto the trajectory of formal decision-making.",

    "968": "In conclusion, Seizing capability is by no means a trajectory that launches mechanistically and automatically; rather, it has been starkly revealed through field evidence to be a highly \u2018processual mechanism\u2019 that awakens only when stringently controlled specific conditions are fully interlocked. This converges upon the powerful scholarly urge that the touchstone for determining whether Dynamic Capabilities have actually been activated within the organizational system must be comprehensively redefined\u2014departing from the retrospective lens of \u2018the presence or absence of outcomes or results\u2019\u2014through the innovative lens of \u2018the initiation of essential procedures and the possibility of their preservation.\u2019",

    "969": "Furthermore, this study complements the existing research stream\u2014which has been accumulated around success cases\u2014by extending into theoretically explicable analytical objects the state in which decisions were not actually made, namely non-decision and non-events.",

    "970": "Practically, this study raises the necessity of reconstituting whether judgments formed after AI utilization training requests have actually been incorporated into the organization\u2019s decision-making structure as the core criterion for outcome conversion. This points to the limitations of approaches that reduce the performance of AI utilization training to educational content or individual learning achievement.",

    "971": "Simultaneously, by explicitly recognizing the limitations of a single-case study and the insider-researcher positionality, it makes clear that the findings of this study should be interpreted not from the perspective of statistical generalization but from the perspective of theoretical generalization aimed at understanding the processual mechanism of the judgment\u2013decision transition.",

    "972": "In sum, this study, by redefining the failure of outcome conversion after AI utilization training requests not as a problem of results but as a problem of process, presents a process-centered extension to Dynamic Capabilities Theory and organizational decision-making research, and positions the organizational phenomenon in which judgments are not converted into decisions as an independent research object.",

    "974": "Recommendations",

    "975": "Chapter 7: Recommendations and Directions for Future Research",

    "976": "The following recommendations are offered regarding the significance of this dissertation. This study critically re-examines the pre-existing implicit assumption that judgments formed within organizations after AI utilization training requests automatically convert into decisions, and repositions such conversion failure not as a matter of individual competency deficits or the limitations of training effectiveness, but as a structural problem of the non-initiation of the processual and institutional conditions required for the activation of Seizing within Dynamic Capabilities Theory.",

    "977": "In particular, this study raises the theoretical and methodological necessity of including the states of non-decision and non-events themselves as legitimate objects of analysis by re-conceptualizing Seizing not as a singular decision act or outcome, but as the entire process through which judgments are incorporated into\u2014or ultimately fail to be incorporated into\u2014the formal decision-making structure.",

    "978": "From this perspective, this study proposes that the approach of evaluating the practical success or failure after AI utilization training requests by individual learning achievement or technical proficiency level be reconsidered. For judgments to trigger actual organizational change, formal pathways through which those judgments can move to decision-making agendas must be institutionally secured, and structural devices\u2014including the clear designation of responsible agents, the establishment of timelines and deadlines, and mechanisms inducing procedure initiation\u2014must be arranged in advance. Therefore, the criterion of evaluation should be placed not on learning outcomes per se, but on the existence of the institutional design enabling the judgment\u2013decision transition.",

    "979": "Viewed from the stratum of macro-level policy and institutional design, AI utilization training requests must be decisively repositioned from the prevailing inertia of dismissing them as transient educational programs at the fragmented operational level to a weighty \u2018institutional event\u2019 capable of disrupting and reorganizing the entire decision-making trajectory of the organizational system. Moreover, structural control mechanisms must be urgently constructed to meticulously monitor under what organizational conditions the vacuum state\u2014in which no substantive decision is gestated and remains adrift\u2014extends its viability or ultimately dissolves. This converges upon the firm practical urge to elevate the very \u2018morass of non-decision\u2019 that had been neglected in the shadows to the status of a legitimate \u2018institutionally managed object\u2019 that the organization can preemptively control and remedy.",

    "980": "In comprehensive assessment, this inquiry thoroughly rejects the attempt to define the fatal abyss of disconnection lying between the initiation of AI utilization training requests and the ultimate generation of organizational performance outcomes through the superficial and outcome-deterministic criterion of \u2018failure of practical implementation.\u2019 Instead, it has comprehensively reinterpreted such an intransigent terrain of stagnation through the sharpest analytical lens\u2014one that clearly illuminates the \u2018essential processual conditions\u2019 that must precede the full awakening of the Seizing mechanism of Dynamic Capabilities Theory.",

    "981": "Such an original reformulation of the concept has achieved the weighty scholarly accomplishment of grafting a thoroughly process-centered perspective onto the previously dominant paradigm of Dynamic Capabilities Theory, thereby presenting a breakthrough for its new evolution. In conclusion, this dissertation erects the most formidable scholarly and policy milestone\u2014one that robustly fuses the practical renewal within the organizational system with the trajectory of future follow-up research\u2014before the academic community and the field, thereby placing a period upon its grand journey.",
}

